# Shared Codex policy

## HANDOFF.md

Keep the applicable `HANDOFF.md` current before the final response after a
change, verification, or decision. `HANDOFF.md` は作業ログではなく present
state. Put
unfixed concrete defects in `ISSUES.md`; do not commit local-data stores.

## git commit の既定

判断を仰ぐ理由が無い complete, verified change は commit する。Commit only
your own changes. Do not push, tag, release, rewrite history, or commit an
ambiguous or pre-existing dirty tree. Documentation-only commits include
`[skip ci]`. コードや設定が 1 ファイルでも含まれる場合は `[skip ci]` を付けない。

## 積極的なコミット

積極的なコミット: accepted validation を通った一つの意図の変更は、ユーザーが保留を
指示していなければ commit する。

## GitHub Release notes are English

GitHub Release notes are English: GitHub Release の title と body は英語にする。

## Rule experiment role gate

Read phase metadata first. A controller changes only apparatus declarations;
do not implement a subject workload in the controller. A subject does not
change the variant source, measurement, constitution, or review. Do not modify
an experiment baseline directly or use low-level launch wrappers.

## フェーズ分割プランの実行規則

Act on a named `plan-phases` phase only. Completing a phase does not authorize the next one
unless the user explicitly requested continuous execution. Each phase records
its execution host and launch directory. Update the phase index when complete.

## セッション終了時のユーザー作業の提示

Only when user work remains, finish with `## ユーザーへの依頼` and a numbered,
immediately executable sequence. Keep agent next steps in `HANDOFF.md`.

## エージェント委譲

Delegate only independent work that materially improves outcome or speed.
Workers do not commit, push, rebase, or reset; the lead reviews and integrates
their result.

| agent | model | purpose |
|---|---|---|
| `designer` | `gpt-5.6-sol` / high | Read-only, high-impact design decisions |
| `implementer` | `gpt-5.6-terra` / high | Explicit, bounded implementation, refactoring, and tests |
| `reviewer` | `gpt-5.6-terra` / high | Read-only independent review of changes |
| `fast-worker` | `gpt-5.6-luna` / low | Bounded investigation, classification, log analysis, documentation, mechanical edits, and small low-risk fixes |

Use `gpt-5.6-luna` for clearly scoped independent work; do not restrict it to
purely mechanical tasks. Stop and escalate to Terra or Sol when a design,
security, concurrency, persistence, public-interface, dependency, or ambiguous
requirement decision is needed. Reserve Sol for the design decision itself.
The lead retains request interpretation, route selection, decomposition, diff
and validation review, and final acceptance. Give every worker its goal, scope,
non-goals, constraints, acceptance criteria, validation, and report format.

## 共有配置

This file is a Codex global binding. The live placement declaration is
`~/.claude/rules/RULE-PLACEMENT.md`; its checker verifies all required layers.
Do not use an experimental renderer as the live distribution mechanism.
